Vendor runtime images are referenced by immutable registry digest and are not
claimed as NPA-published images. NVIDIA's AnomalyGen image fails SkyPilot
bootstrap, so the checked-in restricted `paidf-anomalygen-sky` image builds the
exact Apache-2.0 source revision on digest-pinned public CUDA bases. It belongs
in an operator-controlled registry and may never be published to NPA's public
GHCR namespace without a separate redistribution review. NPA runtime-fetches exact
Apache-2.0 protocol source where the selected vendor service image does not
carry its client, and verifies the fetched commit before execution. All
registered components use S3-compatible object storage for handoffs.
Each run writes `reports/upstream.json` (`npa.paidf.upstream.v1`) so this
adaptation boundary and the exact public revisions travel with its artifacts.

NPA modifies the runtime-fetched paidf-augmentation image writer to honor its
published JPEG output path before the upstream VLM verifier reads that output.
The unmodified writer saves PNG model-response bytes as .jpg, while the verifier
declares image/jpeg. Input preparation likewise normalizes source images to RGB
JPEG and preserves source and prepared hashes. No model or evaluator is replaced.
This Apache-2.0 source adaptation is bound to the exact original and patched
SHA-256 of modules/generation/executors/base.py; unexpected bytes fail closed.
The augmentation report records npa.paidf.upstream-source-adaptation.v1, and both
output and terminal lineage validation require its exact identity. Video output
bytes are unchanged. The declared upstream source revision remains separately
attributed, and model weights remain runtime fetches under the operator's access.

IAA and EVG generation also require restricted operator-built wrappers:
paidf-image-edit-sky and paidf-event-video-sky use exact upstream
vLLM-Omni parent digests listed in the container catalog and add SkyPilot
worker prerequisites, an isolated NPA environment, and argument forwarding. IAA
uses the aligned upstream 0.22.0 release to fix CVE-2026-48746 in the blueprint's
0.20 runtime, preserving the Qwen model revision and image-edit protocol.
EVG retains its generation parent and installs the exact Apache-2.0 NLTK 3.10.3
wheel by SHA-256 to fix CVE-2026-79675, preserving the declared dependency contract.
The AnomalyGen compatibility recipe applies the same wheel after its upstream
requirements. Its separate NPA environment preserves the compiled vendor stack;
AnomalyGen subprocesses explicitly select the vendor interpreter environment.
