The EVG vendor runtime uses Cosmos-1.0-Guardrail, separately from DIG's
Cosmos-Guardrail1. NPA verifies exact payload access, stages the generation and
guardrail snapshots in an isolated revision-bound cache, verifies every cached
path/hash/size against the exact Hugging Face revision manifest, and runs the service offline.
Only the small NLTK data subtree is copied into regular files; model weights
remain in the runtime cache. NLTK 3.10.3 pathsec protections and the original
Cosmos guardrails remain enabled. NPA deliberately changes the upstream EVG
template's extra_params.guardrails=false to true for every request. A private
runtime source overlay makes Qwen3Guard require one complete published safety
verdict and raise on malformed, missing, or duplicate verdicts or inference
exceptions. Safe and Controversial remain allowed; Unsafe remains rejected.
The installed vendor package and real model inference are preserved. The edited
Apache-2.0 cosmos_guardrail/cosmos_guardrail.py source is bound by SHA-256:
  original 117e834a4362ad82748c4146391ab1116039243cfe4cca94954f4c204024daea
  adapted  ab6855b91597e86d8ff57302c323b0df8e88a8bce4d16b3f990a6ee485dd6223
Runtime reports record this adaptation, model revisions, file counts, byte totals,
and content-tree hashes. Enabled guardrails are a request/runtime contract,
not evidence that every input will receive an accepted verdict.

